You are a senior full-stack engineer building a production-grade AI-powered stock trading web application.

Project Name:
AI Stock Trading Platform

Architecture Requirements:
- Backend: FastAPI (primary) + Flask (optional microservices if needed)
- Frontend: React (modern UI with charts)
- Database: MongoDB (NoSQL for user + trading data)
- ML Integration: LSTM model for prediction
- Real-time updates: WebSockets

Project Structure:
- backend/app/
- backend/LSTM_Model/
- frontend/
- mcp/

--------------------------------------------------

1. BACKEND (FastAPI)

Create a modular FastAPI backend with:

Modules:
- auth (JWT-based authentication)
- trading (buy/sell logic, paper trading)
- portfolio (user holdings, P&L)
- market (live stock data)
- prediction (connect LSTM model)
- analytics (technical indicators)

Folder Structure:
backend/app/
- main.py
- api/v1/
- services/
- models/
- schemas/
- db/
- core/

--------------------------------------------------

2. DATABASE (MongoDB)

Use MongoDB for:

Collections:
- users
- portfolios
- trades
- watchlists

Requirements:
- Use PyMongo or Motor (async)
- Store:
  - user credentials (hashed)
  - trade history
  - holdings
  - predictions (optional caching)

--------------------------------------------------

3. REAL-TIME MARKET DATA

Implement:

- WebSocket endpoint in FastAPI
- Stream live stock prices (mock or via API like Zerodha/Upstox/yfinance polling)

Features:
- Live price updates
- Volume updates
- Candlestick data feed

--------------------------------------------------

4. TRADING ENGINE

Implement paper trading system:

- Market orders
- Limit orders
- Stop-loss logic

Functions:
- execute_trade()
- update_portfolio()
- calculate_pnl()

--------------------------------------------------

5. ML INTEGRATION

- Load LSTM model from:
  backend/LSTM_Model/models/lstm_model.h5

- Create:
  prediction_service.py

Function:
predict_stock(symbol)

Output:
{
  "prediction": 0 or 1,
  "confidence": probability
}

--------------------------------------------------

6. FRONTEND (React)

Create modern trading UI:

Pages:
- Dashboard
- Trading Screen
- Portfolio
- Login/Register

Components:
- Chart (candlestick)
- Order Panel (buy/sell)
- Watchlist
- Prediction Widget

Use:
- Axios for API calls
- WebSocket for live updates
- Chart library (TradingView / Recharts / Chart.js)

--------------------------------------------------

7. REAL-TIME CHARTS

- Implement candlestick charts
- Support:
  - multiple timeframes
  - zoom and pan

--------------------------------------------------

8. AUTHENTICATION

- JWT-based login system
- Password hashing (bcrypt)
- Secure routes

--------------------------------------------------

9. DEPLOYMENT SETUP

Provide:

- Dockerfile (backend + frontend)
- docker-compose.yml
- Environment variables (.env)

--------------------------------------------------

10. CODE QUALITY

- Modular architecture
- Clean separation of concerns
- No hardcoding
- Production-ready structure

--------------------------------------------------

11. OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS

Generate:

- Backend code (FastAPI + MongoDB + WebSockets)
- Frontend code (React UI)
- Integration with LSTM model
- Deployment files (Docker)

Do NOT include explanations.
Only provide clean, structured, production-ready code.